// The deliberately-wrong twin for the V5 task-6 array/multiset surface:
// a body that does NOT touch `s`, with a "permutation" post-condition
// that claims the first element's count GREW by one — self-contradictory
// (both sides read the same unchanged multiset, and counts are ≤ N so
// the +1 cannot wrap). REFUTES with a concrete counter-example, pinning
// that `ms_of`/`ms_count` over Array(T, N) are live in post-conditions.
// (The positive direction — the full insertion sort proving sorted +
// permutation — is the valid fixture's job; a body-level bug twin was
// measured and DROPPED: its refute needs a quantified model search z3
// does not finish at any budget, while proves and ground refutes are
// fast.)
pragma(Pragma.Verify);

wrong_perm :: (
  fn(
    s : Array(i64, 8),
    ensures(
      ms_count(ms_of(s), s(i64(0))) == (ms_count(ms_of(old(s)), s(i64(0))) + i64(1))
    )
  ) -> (result : unit)
)({
  first := s(i64(0));
  ()
});
